"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole and launched in Q3 2023. The project has secured strategic partnerships with TechInnovate and expanded its team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms. The executive board approved a $2M budget, though an update later adjusted the project budget to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. Additionally, the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, with further discussions scheduled for meetings in August."
